{1851}{497l
May 22, 1885  18:00 Against my better judgement I've accepted a job from a wealthy dwarf named Hiram Slatebreaker. He claims to be on a mission to find the remains of an ancient king who died in a city called Vorakia on the coast of Vendigroth Province over 2000 years ago. I've never been fond of dwarves, but his money is good.

May 30, 1885  We've departed from Ashbury. The sea is calm and the winds fair. We're following the coastline instead of a more direct approach due to the swirling turbulance around the Isle of Despair. By tomorrow afternoon we should be in sight of Leahbo, then we can turn eastward.

June 1, 1885  16:00 A sudden storm has forced us to put into Leahbo. Being so close to the coast, this was the safest action. Slatebreaker, of course, has been grumbling about the delay. I had to let go of one of my crew, a half-ogre named Hamfist, for provoking a fight, then refusing my order to go below to await punishment.

June 7, 1885  8:15 The skies have finally cleared and we're underway again. Slatebreaker is still complaining about the delay. That dead king has waited for 2000 years to be found, what's a few more days ? There'd better be something at Vorakia besides old bones or I might just have to leave some new ones.

June 10, 1885  19:00 We've just passed the last of the known port cities in the provence. This constant lifeless, bleak coastline is unnerving. It's almost a relief when we spot a sandbar. The dwarves are in good spirits at last. Slatebreaker keeps consulting a journal he has and informing me that we are getting close. We'd better be. By tomorrow we'll be at the edge of the Kolken current.

June 11, 1885  7:00 After a long and heated shouting match with Slatebreaker and his companions we are continuing more or less along the coast, but we're fighting the current every inch of the way. If a storm were to come upon us now, we'd be dashed against the shore for certain. Slatebreaker revealed that where we are headed there's}
{1852}{497l not 1 but 2 long-forgotten cities! It seems that this Vorakia has a younger sister-city named Adia and they're both nestled in the cauldera of a long-extinct coastal volcano. Thus, they've been hidden from those foolish enough to risk the Kolken current. The crafty bastard also let me know that he's willing to turn a blind eye towards anything we might find in Adia, but until the king's body is recovered, Vorakia is not to be touched. Given the high prices that Vendigroth artifacts fetch, we were able to come to an agreement.

June 13, 1885  20:00 Our progress has slowed to a crawl. There are thousands of sandbars in this area and every single one of them seems determined to ground the Sand Witch. We've anchored for the night and come morning, we'll head south by south-east for a while. I don't care that Slatebreaker says we're almost there, I'm heading for deeper water.

June 14, 1885  8:10 We are aground. The ship's unharmed, fortunately, but we are well and truly stuck. From the crow's nest, the lookout was kind enough to reveal that, had we maintained our original course, we would be in calm deep water and that these shallows extend in an arc for almost two miles. Slatebreaker got strangely excited by that information, saying that the south walls of the volcano must have collapsed and the sandbars have formed atop of the rubble. If that's true, then Vorakia must be that tiny ribbon of land that's just out of reach. Damn!

June 30, 1885 20:00 I give up. All the gods must be against us. For 16 days now the entire ship's complement has been laboring to free the Sand Witch but the current washes in fresh sand as fast as we can dig it out. The swiftness of the current precludes any attempt to reach the shore with a launch. One of the two bits of good news is that these waters are teeming with tasty fish and jellyfish. The other is that dwarves rigged a sun-powered distillery, so fresh water is plentiful. Still, at this point, I welcome a storm if it}
{1853}{497l would lift us off this damned shoal.

July 17, 1885 12:00 There's a storm building, but it's going to be coming at us from the north-east. I have a bad feeling that if we do loose, we'll be blown straight into the heart of the Kolken and then become residents of the Isle of Despair. We're ready - as much as we can be.

July 18, 1885 20:00 The storm has hit and it's as bad as I'd feared. After the ship was lifted and dropped a few hundred times, she finally broke loose. We are now being pushed straight into the Kolken. May the gods have mercy on us all.

July 22, 1885 20:00 The hell-sent storm is beginning to subside. Perhaps tomorrow I will be able to get a reading and determine just how close to Despair we are now. We are busy with repairs to the rigging and attempting to steer a more northerly course.

July 23, 1885 15:30 I finally have our location and it's not good. We are dangerously close to the north-east tip of Despair. I'm about to order a very risky manuever that should throw us into one of the charted vortexes and from there we can break free and return to port.

July 31, 1885 16:00 We have finally broken free of the current and are about to make land-fall. I never thought I'd be glad to see lifeless desert, but right now the Vendigroth Wastes seem like paradise.

August 1, 1885 12:00 This is an accursed place! Our scouting party caught the attention of a bizarre purplish half-spider, half-woman demon armed with a bow. Jonsey was wounded but everyone managed to make it back to the ship alive. As quickly as possible, we made ready and lifted anchor. Even Slatebreaker and his companions pitched in.

August 5, 1885 10:00 After four days of picking our way along the coast, we are drawing near the treacherous shoals again. This time, we shall anchor well off shore and scout a path with the dinghy.

August 5, 1885 14:00 A course has been laid out and well-marked. We are about to enter Vorakia's harbor. It would seem the dwarf's}
{1854}{497l assessment that the cauldera's walls had collapsed may indeed be accurate, as evidence abounds of seamounts ringing the coastline. Already, a small range of jagged ridges which extend to the water are within sight.

August 6, 1885 10:45 We have arrived at the twin cities. A crumbling jetty has provided us with a safe place to moor the ship. Stone ruins and metal-clad buildings abound at this site and everyone is eager to begin exploration of this amazing place. Everyone who's going ashore will be heavily armed and I've sent two men into the crow's nest. Just because a place looks dead doesn't mean that it's lifeless.

August 6, 1885 20:00 We have finished our initial scouting of the cities. They are both in a remarkable state of presesrvation. Even the iron bridge that spans the marsh is structurally sound. Amazing. There are at least two roads leading out of the bowl and into the wastes. Both are in Adia, with one at the north edge of the bowl, almost due north of our location, and the other at the far east edge of the shoreline. Slatebreaker was good enough to point out three places close to the ship where we should find some sort of treasure. Trust a dwarf to know where to dig. He and his companions promptly decided that one large structure in Vorakia would be where they began their search. 
Also - it seems we are not the first to find this forgotten place. Although the newer city is as uninhabited as it appears, other than common desert lizards and spiders, the older city on the west side of the marsh has a walled structure that is obviously quite a bit newer. This structure is in ruins, with holes in the outer walls and a collapsed roof. It lies to the far west of the city and beside what might be a passage to the outside world. 
The scouting party reported that as they entered the enclosure, one of the men was positive he heard the grinding buzz of a skeletal warrior. They made a hasty retreat and seem to have avoided drawing the damned}
{1855}{497l things' attention. Tonight, we'll know for certain. Even the dwarves are standing guard.
August 7, 1885 20:00 The foul things in the west ruins seem to be ignoring us as nothing bothered us during the night. Today we made excellent progress at clearing the stairwell of a vast belltower and created a pit beside a shop. The loose soil makes for easy digging and the work went quickly. Slatebreaker and company are practically foaming at the mouth to get at the large ruin in Vorakia, but acknowledged the need for someone to watch their backs. 
As soon as these three locations are excavated, I'll spare a man or two for them. Tomorrow morning, we'll breach the last barrier of the tower and the basement wall and see what can be found.

August 8, 1885 19:30 Success at last! The tower stairs lead directly into a small circular room and from there into a much larger room that was positively brimming with Vendigrothian furniture and artifacts. It had to have been the city hall. The second excavation revealed a smallish basement with several packing crates filled with obviously ancient but more common items. Perhaps it was a general store. 
Most of these treasures are now safely within our hold and work shall begin on the third spot in the morning.

August 9, 1885 18:00 There is a disturbing development. It seems that the current in the harbor is trying to form a sand bar around the ship. We'll have to leave here soon or risk becoming grounded. I sent two men along with the dwarves into Vorakia and upon their return, Slate-breaker reported that they had broken into a buried chamber beneath. As the air in the chamber was quite foul, the dwarves decided to allow it to air out overnight before entering. 
The last treasures from the Adia city hall are now on board and the third pit is almost fully dug. The stonework on the third location is remarkably intact and may require blasting to breach. Even if that room is empty this will be a most profitable voyage. To be sure,}
{1856}{497l I plan to make many more trips to this untapped goldmine. Yes indeed.

August 10, 1885 This may be my last entry. Shortly after Slatebreaker had departed for Vorakia, Jonsey set off the charges at the third dig. The wall was breached revealing a small room, but the explosion seems to have disturbed every evil thing for a hundred miles! Hordes of spiders and those spider-demons came pouring out of the mountains and every hole and nook in the area. My men fought valiantly but were quickly overwhelmed and torn limb form limb. 
I was unable to see anything of Slatebreaker or his team, as I, my first mate and the two remaining crewmen were quickly driven onto the ship. 
I fear the worse for them. 
I ran below to get more ammo and that's when the deck was overrun by the demons. 
The screams! Gods! I've never heard men scream like that.
 
Some places were never meant to be rediscovered and this is one of them. Get out while you can and tell the world to avoid this accursed place at any and all costs. 
Let it remain forgotten.

Soon the demons will find their way below. 
I'm ready for them. 

They are here______
}
