 1) The primary focus of this release is the Vormantown adventure. 
You can find it at Ivory Lake.

This addition is still over 90% original. I added some dim lighting for the back rooms at the Vorman mansion, bypassed the end screens, created a bit of final dialog with Shackleford to end the adventure, and reset two teleports to a more logical location.

Note: Due to the sheer volume of level-ups that's built-in, getting your favorite early-game followers before you go to Vormantown would be a good idea.

 2) Began adding team a's hack fixes and suggestions. (40 changes!) This has helped a lot. This includes the night-time toggle-off for the halflings.
 3) Began adding elements of Drog Black Tooth's Unofficial Bug-fix (Added 234 fixes!). Some things are incompatable with my hack. Those will have to be left out. Others didn't want to work immediately and will be tested again later.
 4) Made bug or scene fixes from Terra-Arcanum or Codex postings. (31 listed so far!) 
 5) Reset the Vortahm to use stock spells so that your followers have a better chance of surviving the adventure.
 6) Altered the XP level-up amounts. Starting at level 12, the amounts needed were boosted to 1.75%. This will help offset the effects all the new adventures are having on the leveling schemes.
 7) Replaced the sound clip used for the halflings with the complete song "Concerning Hobbits".
 8) Added a new hobbit-hole behind the market.
 9) Added T'e'MHbIu` s Manual View Patch. You can now see at a glance what kind of tech manual is in your inventory.
10) Added the most recent version of Virgil's dialog with a map-marking cheat.
11) Removed most of the unnecessary items from the Molochean Hand.
12) Added a townmap to Vaselan.}
{1901}{37l
13) Reset the Shrouded Hills gypsy to the stock game inventory.
14) Reset the Orc Bandits' loot to simpler tech items.
15) Removed the Sword of Sickness and Crushing Hammer from the Shrouded Hills Gypsy's initial inventory. 
16) Added the No-cd Arcanum.exe and Drog's CleanCache.bat to the download.
17) Added a Divine Fire Pistol to Ashbury. A magickal gun with 20-30 normal damage + fireball!
18) Reset the Kill On Sight flags for the Poison Arachnids at the Iron Clan.
19) Reset description of Hadrian from Half-ogre guard to gnome priest.
20) Acted on Darkform's debug postings - but I forgot to keep count. Sorry! I'll call it 20 - If I'm wrong let me know. (smile)
21) Added a ton of traps to the Iron Clan.
22) Fixed the description on a painting at the Black Root Mayor's house.

If you kept count, that's 343 bug, scene, hack, and dialog changes added to this release. Wow!


Helpful hints: 

In the Spider Cave, each large spider has an ampule of venom that can be combined with a Kadura Stem for 3 poison cures.

There is a 1 in 10 chance when purchasing the hobbit-hole, if you try running straight down to Frigo's place, he will not appear after you return and do the "Where's Frigo?" runaround. Solution: If you do not want to replay the scene from an earlier save, return to the For Sale place and exit the town through the gap in the wall. Advance time one day, then re-enter the town, read the sign, and follow the links.

In Plainwicke, there are numerous black spiders in the banana groves. Kill them to level up before battling the Vortahm.

At Acererak's Tomb, if you have a large party with Virgil, load his inventory with fatigue potions. He'll need it for the poison gas areas.

Enjoy the adventures!

Bryan E. Taylor aka: rroyo}

