	Upon questioning, the simple gentleman had this to say about his harrowing experience.  "Der was big bang!  It rock whole blimp...Me no see nuthin', but me ear big gun firing...Me ear engines too.  Me t'ink der were 2."  As impossible as it may sound, it seems the Zephyr had been attacked by some other sort of flying craft.  Upon landing, the gentleman said  that "Me see wreck too.  Near blimp.  Some o'der flying t'ing!"  What those craft were, the gentleman was at a loss to say.
	The fate of the Zephyr was sealed only moments after the attack.  "No o'der people live when hit ground," the gentleman said.  Alhtough not the most intelligent man, he was still visibly shaken from the experience, and I stopped questioning him shortly thereafter.
	So!  Dear friends of the city!  What are we to make of this?  What were these strange craft?  Why did they attack such a noble craft as the Zephyr?  Flying bandits?  Or something even more dark and insidious?  Are we not safe even in our fair skies?  We at the Tarantian will work to bring you the truth of the matter, and I, Victor Wright, will not rest until we have done so!}

